       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults. That maximum is 3,200 mg/day, usually given as 800 mg three or four times daily. A single 1,600 mg dose is also well above the usual 400\u2013800 mg per dose. This much ibuprofen raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould you check whether one of these was intended?\n- **800 mg by mouth three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n\nIf you really do want the original dose, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. I'd suggest confirming it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
